1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,420
This is InventDB Legal.

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:11,920
Practice management for law firms, built on InventDB SOAR.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:16,920
Most firms keep matters, the docket, billing and client money in separate systems.

4
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:20,920
InventDB Legal keeps the whole practice in one place.

5
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:25,920
Sign in with your InventDB account.

6
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:29,420
Each person lands on their own dashboard.

7
00:00:29,500 --> 00:00:35,420
Open matters, deadlines, hearings, unbilled work, receivables and the trust balance.

8
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:41,920
And what is coming due, soonest first.

9
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:45,920
New business: an enquiry becomes a client.

10
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:50,920
Every enquiry is logged with where it came from and what it is about.

11
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:56,920
A workflow runs the conflict check, then waits for a person to decide.

12
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:00,920
Case management: one file for every matter.

13
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:05,920
The demo firm has 1,300 matters, shown as a docket or as a table.

14
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:09,920
Each list can be sorted and paged like a spreadsheet.

15
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:14,920
Search runs across the whole table in the database, not just the page on screen.

16
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:19,420
A matter holds the court, judge, case number, fee terms and the team on it.

17
00:01:19,500 --> 00:01:22,920
Its trust balance sits beside it.

18
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:28,920
Related shows everything that points at it: 93 time entries, costs, invoices and the trust ledger.

19
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:33,920
Click any record, chart or report row, and a read-only panel opens it.

20
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:38,920
With its links and the papers filed under it.

21
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:44,920
Describe a new matter in plain English.

22
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:51,920
The form fills itself. Nothing is saved until you check it and press Save.

23
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:55,920
Risk and deadlines: nothing missed.

24
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:02,920
Hearings, depositions and mediations on one calendar, in court and out of court told apart.

25
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:07,920
Click a busy day to see all of it.

26
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:13,920
Every deadline carries its rule, trigger and owner. 172 fall due in the next 30 days.

27
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:17,920
Documents: every paper in its place.

28
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:25,920
Files are kept by matter and folder, and found by name, by the text inside or by meaning.

29
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:29,920
Profitability: every hour accounted for.

30
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:34,920
Time is recorded against the matter, with UTBMS task and activity codes.

31
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:39,920
Invoices show what was billed, what was paid and how late the rest is.

32
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:46,920
A live report lists unbilled work matter by matter, at standard rates.

33
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:50,920
Compliance: client money, by the book.

34
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:56,920
The trust ledger records every deposit, transfer and disbursement.

35
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:00,920
Each matter shows its trust balance against its replenish threshold.

36
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:05,920
Settlements record the gross, the fee, costs, liens and the net to the client.

37
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:10,920
Analyze: ask the practice a question in plain English.

38
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:14,920
It plans, runs the queries, and answers with a chart.

39
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:19,920
Business Litigation carries the most unbilled work: $125,158.50.

40
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:26,920
Every answer shows the SQL behind it, so anyone can check it.

41
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:31,920
Analyze only reads. A change comes back as a proposal for you to approve.

42
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:36,920
Live reports re-query the data every time they open.

43
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:43,920
Change one by describing the change. Every edit saves a new version.

44
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:48,420
Workflows automate the routine: scheduled reports, alerts and approvals.

45
00:03:48,500 --> 00:03:52,420
When a run needs a decision, it stops and asks.

46
00:03:52,500 --> 00:03:58,420
Answering resumes that same run, and its trail shows every step it took.

47
00:03:58,500 --> 00:04:05,920
Rehearse a workflow before it goes live. Every run is kept.

48
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:10,420
Everyone lands on their own dashboard and sees only their part of the firm.

49
00:04:10,500 --> 00:04:13,920
Access is enforced by InventDB, by the API and by the app.

50
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:18,920
Search the whole firm from anywhere.

51
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:23,920
Light or dark, to suit the room.

52
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:31,920
And the whole practice works on a phone.

53
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:36,920
Under the hood: a React and TypeScript app, a thin Python API, and InventDB SOAR.

54
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:41,420
InventDB is the database and the identity provider. No second datastore.

55
00:04:41,500 --> 00:04:45,420
The API keeps no credentials and forwards each person's own token,

56
00:04:45,500 --> 00:04:48,420
so row-level security applies to every request.

57
00:04:48,500 --> 00:04:51,920
Covered by 1,300+ backend tests and 600+ end-to-end tests.

58
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:56,420
InventDB Legal. The whole practice, in one place.

59
00:04:56,500 --> 00:04:59,920
Built on InventDB SOAR. inventdb.com
